 "notes": {
  "tech": "Thread proposed 2 (2026-10-11): Footwear (owned names): WaffleCup vulcanised cupsole (about page, 2012), PopCush soles, Duracap (Old Skool icon page); GORE-TEX on shoes (licensed, listing titles). Men's clothing: no named fabric technology; generic DWR coating and 2-layer 10,000mm shells on snow pieces only; \"Vans Checkerboard Globe Materials\" is a sourcing label, not a fabric — footwear: owned (WaffleCup, PopCush, Duracap) plus licensed GORE-TEX; apparel: none named; share of range men's clothing: DWR or 2-layer waterproof shell stated on a handful of the 243 s. Seated as proposed, pending ruling.",
  "craft": "Thread proposed 2 (2026-10-11): The heritage is dated and placed (Van Doren Rubber Company, Anaheim, 16 March 1966), but VF's FY2026 10-K sources products primarily from about 216 independent contractor factories and lists no plants. No men's clothing page names a maker or mill, and none states a country. The process story is footwear construction only (vulcanised soles, WaffleCup). Heritage with no current verifiable making is  Seated as proposed, pending ruling.",
